WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:02.480
Excuse me.

00:02.480 --> 00:06.080
The very beautiful, but very dangerous, Takasu-san asked me to be her boyfriend,

00:06.080 --> 00:09.800
and I had to join a student council
comprised of strange people.

00:09.800 --> 00:12.220
And now the world’s in danger?

00:12.220 --> 00:14.460
I don’t know what’s going on,

00:15.290 --> 00:17.360
but I’ll keep on going!

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

02:00.470 --> 02:01.980
<i>The world’s in danger?</i>

02:02.520 --> 02:04.190
<i>I don’t know what’s happening,</i>

02:04.190 --> 02:07.770
<i>but I’m sure it’s something bad.</i>

02:08.770 --> 02:13.030
Approaching final stop. Beatrice
University High School.

02:13.030 --> 02:16.190
Beatrice University High School.

02:16.190 --> 02:21.200
The Astral Fire Recovery Operation

02:34.300 --> 02:35.460
Takasu Ayako Team Two Only

02:36.000 --> 02:36.930
Takasu-san!

02:47.900 --> 02:49.270
Takasu-san?

02:51.540 --> 02:52.910
Ayako!

02:52.910 --> 02:54.820
Have you calmed down?

02:57.320 --> 02:59.370
Like hell I have!

02:59.370 --> 03:02.230
Do you have any idea how long it took me

03:02.230 --> 03:05.080
to develop that Astral Fire...

03:05.900 --> 03:09.040
Um, good morning.

03:09.040 --> 03:10.800
I’m getting a photo.

03:11.460 --> 03:14.790
M-M-M-M-Mamo...

03:14.790 --> 03:17.070
Man, that really worked.

03:17.070 --> 03:19.270
Great work, Mamoru-kun.

03:19.270 --> 03:21.840
You saved the world.

03:23.470 --> 03:27.180
I was right to have you join the Student Council.

03:27.180 --> 03:31.020
You’re perfect for taming the wild beast that is Ayako...

03:32.690 --> 03:33.750
<i>No!</i>

03:37.290 --> 03:38.440
No...

03:41.300 --> 03:43.700
Student Council President!

03:44.900 --> 03:47.970
A nice blow, filled with love...

03:49.840 --> 03:51.260
Brother!

03:51.260 --> 03:54.330
Don’t die on me!

03:55.250 --> 03:57.610
The Astral Fire was stolen?

03:58.810 --> 04:00.750
They hit the security’s weak points,

04:00.750 --> 04:03.590
and made a beeline to the room.

04:03.590 --> 04:08.320
And signs suggest they used
beatrice to disarm the traps.

04:08.320 --> 04:09.800
Beatrice?

04:09.800 --> 04:11.390
Then the culprit is...

04:11.390 --> 04:14.410
There are a lot of issues to consider.

04:14.410 --> 04:18.640
But our first priority is to recover the Astral Fire.

04:18.640 --> 04:19.230
Ayako.

04:20.210 --> 04:21.740
Gladly.

04:21.740 --> 04:23.240
I’ll take care of this fast.

04:23.240 --> 04:25.000
You, too, Mamoru-san.

04:25.000 --> 04:26.610
We’re counting on you.

04:26.610 --> 04:27.660
OK!

04:29.200 --> 04:31.730
With Ayako there, you’ll be in no danger.

04:31.730 --> 04:35.150
Do your best to keep the city safe.

04:35.150 --> 04:36.780
W-Wait!

04:36.780 --> 04:39.010
Not happening.

04:39.010 --> 04:40.530
Well, I won’t force him–

04:40.530 --> 04:41.370
I’ll go!

04:41.990 --> 04:44.520
Takasu-san, please.

04:44.520 --> 04:46.630
Take me with you.

04:47.460 --> 04:48.700
Why?

04:48.700 --> 04:52.680
I want to know more about you!

04:52.680 --> 04:54.980
Gasp...

04:55.350 --> 04:56.490
Mamoru...

05:00.400 --> 05:02.700
Clap Clap Clap

05:02.880 --> 05:04.130
Interesting.

05:04.130 --> 05:05.410
You’re great, Mamoru-kun.

05:08.000 --> 05:10.110
OK, let’s go together.

05:10.110 --> 05:11.340
Really?

05:11.340 --> 05:13.980
Yeah. Wait just a second.

05:13.980 --> 05:16.420
I have something I need to do.

05:16.420 --> 05:19.820
I’m sure she wants to freshen up.

05:19.820 --> 05:23.120
It’s a date with her beloved Mamoru-san.

05:23.120 --> 05:26.700
She’d be embarrassed if she didn’t look her best.

05:30.070 --> 05:31.540
Stop it!

05:31.540 --> 05:33.720
Please stop it!

05:35.250 --> 05:35.950
Danger!

05:37.230 --> 05:38.230
Bingo!

05:41.110 --> 05:43.430
OK, see you around lunchtime.

05:43.430 --> 05:45.340
If you’re going to be late, let me know.

05:45.340 --> 05:46.140
OK.

05:46.140 --> 05:47.360
I’ll be fine.

05:47.360 --> 05:49.620
I won’t be late.

06:00.270 --> 06:01.640
Yuuka-san?

06:07.850 --> 06:08.920
J-Just happened...

06:08.920 --> 06:10.470
Just happened to be passing by!

06:10.470 --> 06:13.620
I know nothing about the Astral Fire being stolen...

06:13.620 --> 06:15.140
Um, Yuuka-san.

06:16.870 --> 06:19.520
Something has bothered me since yesterday.

06:19.520 --> 06:20.110
Al...

06:21.940 --> 06:23.400
Al!

06:24.880 --> 06:25.690
Yuuka-san...

06:31.470 --> 06:33.030
Yuuka-san.

06:35.510 --> 06:37.120
This is Al.

06:38.460 --> 06:40.050
He’s cute!

06:40.050 --> 06:41.030
Isn’t he?

06:41.030 --> 06:44.940
He’s so smart. And if you go boo, he goes woof.

06:44.940 --> 06:49.400
And if you squeeze him, he goes whuff.
And if you go myunyunyu...

06:54.460 --> 06:56.440
They threatened me.

06:56.440 --> 07:01.030
They said if I wanted him back,
I had to bring them the Astral Fire...

07:01.850 --> 07:07.450
I thought it’d be all right.
Takasu-san wouldn’t ever lose to anyone.

07:07.450 --> 07:11.450
But it hurts, betraying everyone...

07:11.450 --> 07:12.970
Yuuka-san.

07:12.970 --> 07:16.340
But they didn’t give him back.

07:16.340 --> 07:18.440
Al, I’m sorry.

07:18.440 --> 07:20.520
I’m such a screw-up!

07:20.520 --> 07:21.380
So...

07:23.380 --> 07:25.340
Leave it to me.

07:26.040 --> 07:29.620
Ayako-san and I will find the person behind this.

07:29.620 --> 07:33.000
I may not be able to do much,

07:33.000 --> 07:35.530
but I’ll be sure to bring him back.

07:37.250 --> 07:38.560
Mamoru-san...

07:45.470 --> 07:49.360
So why are we here?

07:49.360 --> 07:51.770
You can’t fight on an empty stomach.

07:51.770 --> 07:53.670
Mamor—

07:53.670 --> 07:55.350
Don’t you want dessert?

07:55.350 --> 07:56.600
I’m fine.

07:56.600 --> 08:00.250
Sugar’s good because you can
quickly turn it into energy.

08:01.140 --> 08:04.450
There’s a shortcake, Mamor—

08:04.450 --> 08:07.130
You like shortcake, right?

08:08.180 --> 08:09.470
How did you know?

08:09.470 --> 08:11.900
Oh, right! The survey...

08:11.900 --> 08:15.640
S-Speaking of the survey...

08:16.600 --> 08:18.120
I-It’s OK.

08:18.120 --> 08:20.380
Everyone already read it.

08:20.380 --> 08:23.490
Those guys need to learn some things about privacy.

08:23.490 --> 08:26.060
I haven’t even read it yet!

08:26.770 --> 08:28.820
Takasu-san, what’s wrong?

08:31.390 --> 08:34.900
M-M-M-M-Mamoru?

08:34.900 --> 08:35.490
Yes?

08:39.330 --> 08:41.900
M-Mamoru...

08:41.900 --> 08:44.830
A-A-Aaah!

08:46.690 --> 08:47.570
Takasu-san.

08:51.480 --> 08:52.380
Aaah!

08:53.670 --> 08:54.810
Aah...

08:58.800 --> 09:01.940
I got a nice shot of him with his mouth open.

09:01.940 --> 09:04.280
Love’s a beautiful thing.

09:04.280 --> 09:06.820
It’s changed Ayako so much...

09:06.820 --> 09:10.830
What are you guys doing here?

09:10.830 --> 09:13.080
Coincidences happen.

09:13.080 --> 09:16.430
Yeah. We got to see Ayako go, “Aah!”

09:16.430 --> 09:18.930
I thought my eyeballs would pop out of my skull.

09:21.160 --> 09:25.050
You didn’t learn your lesson this morning!

09:29.170 --> 09:31.180
Another nice shot.

09:31.180 --> 09:33.630
Y-Yay!

09:38.470 --> 09:41.180
I wonder if they’re OK...

09:41.180 --> 09:46.810
If that were enough to kill them,
I’d lead a peaceful life.

09:48.030 --> 09:51.200
Um, Takasu-san, where are we going?

09:51.200 --> 09:54.500
I’m the one who made the Astral Fire.

09:54.500 --> 09:56.870
I can sense it.

09:56.870 --> 09:58.910
The beatrice tells me.

10:00.370 --> 10:01.570
Are you still anxious?

10:01.570 --> 10:07.380
No. Only, I’ve never chased a criminal
or anything like that before.

10:07.380 --> 10:09.480
It just makes me nervous is all.

10:15.700 --> 10:17.380
I’ll protect you, Mamoru.

10:23.240 --> 10:24.310
What’s wrong?

10:24.310 --> 10:25.950
Nothing...

10:26.830 --> 10:29.570
Is it boring, being with me?

10:30.420 --> 10:32.610
No, not at all! Really!

10:36.390 --> 10:38.150
Um, hey.

10:38.150 --> 10:39.050
Yeah?

10:39.050 --> 10:43.520
I’d like to hear your answer.

10:45.250 --> 10:47.740
This really isn’t the time, is it?

10:47.740 --> 10:49.260
I’m sorry.

10:49.260 --> 10:54.220
But... There really isn’t much
chance for us to be alone.

10:56.130 --> 10:59.200
You really don’t have to.

10:59.200 --> 11:01.260
But...

11:01.960 --> 11:04.820
I want to hear it.

11:07.320 --> 11:09.910
<i>I... But...</i>

11:12.780 --> 11:15.380
<i>But I’m not good enough.</i>

11:15.380 --> 11:20.740
<i>At times like these, all I can do
is have her protect me.</i>

11:26.650 --> 11:28.030
Takasu-san, over there!

11:31.840 --> 11:37.170
You’re going to pay for ruining my perfect chance...

11:38.340 --> 11:39.510
Takasu-san!

11:39.510 --> 11:41.640
You wait here!

12:15.630 --> 12:17.540
There’s no point in hiding.

12:17.540 --> 12:20.650
The beatrice is on my side.

12:20.650 --> 12:24.230
It’ll tell me where you are, no matter where you hide.

12:25.520 --> 12:26.850
I see.

12:26.850 --> 12:32.630
Then I just need to get rid of all
the beatrice around here.

12:33.230 --> 12:36.900
Um, excuse me!

12:49.240 --> 12:52.410
The beatrice disappeared...

12:52.410 --> 12:56.540
Using beatrice to erase the surrounding beatrice...

12:56.540 --> 13:00.880
Every normal, powerless person has thought of that.

13:00.880 --> 13:05.130
You’ll pay for ruining my plan three years ago,

13:05.130 --> 13:07.050
you accursed witch!

13:08.080 --> 13:10.760
You abominable witch!

13:17.550 --> 13:19.020
Takasu-san!

13:20.400 --> 13:23.490
Look at you, Witch Beatrice!

13:27.680 --> 13:28.700
What?

13:28.700 --> 13:33.240
Even without the beatrice,
it will take more than a gun to hurt me.

13:34.160 --> 13:35.090
Takasu-san!

13:36.170 --> 13:37.710
Take this!

13:40.590 --> 13:43.800
You’re just going to run, Witch Beatrice?

13:44.620 --> 13:48.340
Without beatrice, even a witch is helpless as a baby.

13:48.340 --> 13:51.670
Today, I’ll have my revenge!

13:52.270 --> 13:53.880
<i>That’s right.</i>

13:53.880 --> 13:57.540
<i>If I went out there, I’d just slow her down.</i>

13:57.540 --> 14:00.630
<i>So what can I do?</i>

14:05.720 --> 14:07.760
Al-kun! No!

14:07.760 --> 14:08.490
Mamoru!

14:11.090 --> 14:12.130
Who’s there?

14:13.590 --> 14:16.260
You with the witch?

14:20.970 --> 14:22.640
No!

14:34.520 --> 14:35.960
Takasu-san!

14:41.470 --> 14:42.490
Takasu-san?

14:49.360 --> 14:52.000
<i>Takasu-san’s a girl.</i>

14:52.000 --> 14:55.290
<i>No matter how strong she is. Or how famous she is.</i>

14:55.730 --> 14:57.010
<i>And yet...</i>

14:59.530 --> 15:02.070
<i>And yet, I...</i>

15:02.820 --> 15:04.900
<i>Why did I hesitate?</i>

15:06.700 --> 15:09.380
<i>I’m sorry, Takasu-san.</i>

15:09.380 --> 15:11.330
Are you a beatrice user?

15:13.180 --> 15:16.760
Too bad. There isn’t any beatrice here.

15:16.760 --> 15:19.560
Except for this Astral Fire!

15:21.610 --> 15:23.010
Please stop it!

15:28.840 --> 15:32.640
You just lie there and watch the witch die.

15:32.640 --> 15:36.930
Burn away at the hands of your own invention!

15:38.070 --> 15:39.040
Stop it...

15:39.040 --> 15:41.050
Takasu Ayako!

15:43.420 --> 15:44.630
Stop it.

15:46.080 --> 15:48.060
Stop it!

15:54.290 --> 15:55.340
It’s hot!

15:55.340 --> 15:56.260
Someone help me!

16:13.390 --> 16:14.380
Mamoru...

16:15.600 --> 16:16.930
You’re awake.

16:16.930 --> 16:18.780
Where am I?

16:18.780 --> 16:20.600
Don’t worry.

16:20.600 --> 16:22.900
I’m driving you to school.

16:24.390 --> 16:25.060
Oh, right!

16:25.060 --> 16:26.880
Takasu-san was hurt!

16:26.890 --> 16:28.700
Don’t worry.

16:28.700 --> 16:32.430
I use beatrice to strengthen my body.

16:32.430 --> 16:36.300
A wound like that heals easily.

16:36.300 --> 16:42.200
But when I got shot,
I lost consciousness from the shock.

16:42.200 --> 16:44.380
I see.

16:44.380 --> 16:46.610
Um, what happened to the criminal?

16:46.610 --> 16:48.930
We handed him over to the police.

16:48.930 --> 16:51.150
It’s all thanks to you.

16:51.150 --> 16:55.660
You used beatrice to save me.

16:55.660 --> 16:57.660
I used beatrice?

16:57.660 --> 16:58.960
No way...

16:58.960 --> 17:05.420
He used beatrice to eliminate all
the ambient beatrice from that room.

17:06.620 --> 17:11.810
But when I woke up, the beatrice was there.

17:11.810 --> 17:14.880
So where did it come from?

17:14.880 --> 17:18.970
All living things possess beatrice.

17:19.590 --> 17:23.560
You used his body’s beatrice

17:23.560 --> 17:27.350
to protect me, didn’t you?

17:29.650 --> 17:31.390
No, I didn’t...

17:31.390 --> 17:32.660
I didn’t do anything.

17:32.660 --> 17:34.550
Thank you, Mamoru.

17:46.720 --> 17:49.640
I’m so... I’m sorry!

17:49.640 --> 17:52.010
Sh-She couldn’t help it!

17:52.010 --> 17:53.880
Al-kun was taken hostage.

17:57.060 --> 17:59.020
Thank you for telling us.

17:59.790 --> 18:03.930
You were freaking out so obviously,
anyone could’ve told.

18:03.930 --> 18:08.230
We all knew you were involved from the start.

18:08.230 --> 18:12.130
We didn’t want to call you out.

18:12.130 --> 18:15.740
You’re one of us, after all.

18:17.200 --> 18:20.010
All’s well that ends well.

18:17.690 --> 18:22.590
And so, we were sure you’d
tell us the truth one day.

18:22.590 --> 18:23.830
President...

18:23.830 --> 18:27.340
And we had insurance, too.

18:27.340 --> 18:31.960
The Astral Fire they stole was a fake
that could only be used once.

18:31.960 --> 18:34.990
If worst came to worst, only Ayako would die.

18:36.750 --> 18:40.720
I changed it without telling you.

18:40.720 --> 18:43.530
They say if you want to trick your enemies,
you should start by tricking your friends.

18:43.530 --> 18:45.670
Brother, you’re so smart!

18:45.670 --> 18:46.970
President...

18:46.970 --> 18:50.100
What you’re saying totally
contradicts what you said earlier.

18:50.100 --> 18:53.230
Now, then! What shall we do
about Yuuka’s punishment?

18:53.230 --> 18:54.890
As a student council member,

18:54.890 --> 18:57.340
it’s something she has to go through.
It’s in the rules.

18:57.340 --> 18:59.180
I’ve already decided.

19:00.030 --> 19:02.610
How about a whack on the head?

19:02.610 --> 19:03.780
Y-Yes!

19:08.260 --> 19:10.700
Then punch me, too!

19:10.700 --> 19:13.710
I knew, and I didn’t say anything!

19:14.610 --> 19:16.000
Mamoru...

19:19.990 --> 19:23.940
And I didn’t tell you about switching the Astral Fire.

19:23.940 --> 19:25.930
Give me a light one...

19:27.610 --> 19:28.400
Galactica Magnum

19:28.400 --> 19:33.250
Shione, I’m approving additional repair funds!

19:42.220 --> 19:43.990
We’re lucky.

19:43.990 --> 19:47.040
We get to see the cherry blossoms
flowering twice this year.

19:48.150 --> 19:49.550
I’m sorry...

19:50.990 --> 19:53.030
I was overconfident.

19:53.030 --> 19:57.710
I was certain that no matter who attacked me...
When, where, or with what...

19:57.710 --> 20:00.720
I could beat them easily.

20:01.400 --> 20:02.680
And yet...

20:03.180 --> 20:09.680
When you were there, my mind went totally blank.

20:10.500 --> 20:14.480
And I was going to protect you...

20:14.480 --> 20:16.210
Takasu-san...

20:16.680 --> 20:21.570
If you’re with me, you may be put in danger again.

20:21.570 --> 20:24.910
But I...

20:24.910 --> 20:27.970
I’ve lost that confidence.

20:28.960 --> 20:30.200
So...

20:30.930 --> 20:33.550
So about what I said...

20:33.550 --> 20:34.910
Wait!

20:34.910 --> 20:39.180
Can I go first?

20:40.030 --> 20:43.670
I didn’t have any confidence, either.

20:43.670 --> 20:46.950
I thought I wasn’t worthy of you.

20:46.950 --> 20:49.930
I thought I’d just cause trouble...

20:49.930 --> 20:51.090
Mamoru...

20:51.090 --> 20:56.660
But I thought to myself that if I could use beatrice, too,

20:56.660 --> 21:01.870
then I’ll be confident in myself someday...

21:02.900 --> 21:07.570
That I can watch over you, by your side.

21:12.500 --> 21:13.890
Takasu-san...

21:14.780 --> 21:16.120
Ayako-san!

21:19.540 --> 21:22.620
Please be my girlfriend.

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:16.570 --> 23:22.760
Congratulations to Yoshimura-kun for joining the Student Council!

23:22.760 --> 23:24.290
An exciting hide-and-seek game!

23:24.290 --> 23:26.110
Be nice to the Venus de Milo...

23:26.110 --> 23:30.940
Wait, that pun sucked.

23:30.940 --> 23:34.830
Shione wrote it? I thought so.

23:34.830 --> 23:38.930
Man, her hairstyle’s bad enough already!

23:39.510 --> 23:42.580
Next time: The Student Council in the Prime of Youth.

23:40.290 --> 23:43.980
The Student Council in the Prime of Youth
